+/*
+ * SWEET audio, Poco F1 (SDM845): the Hexagon ADSP's audio services and the TAS2559/TAS2560 speaker amplifiers,
+ * behind the IOKit service SweetAudio (iokit/Kernel/arm/SweetAudio.cpp) that audiomxd's HAL plug-in
+ * (audio/hal/SweetAudio.driver in the Bergamota repo) drives. Patch 1158. At boot only the service is
+ * published; the hardware starts with the first client START or `sweetsysctl kern.sweet_audio_ctl=N`, and
+ * kern.sweet_audio reports where it got. Every step logs "SWEET AUDIO:".
+ *
+ *   ADSP   PAS 1 through TrustZone: adsp.mbn (ELF32, relocatable) into adsp_mem 0x8c500000 (30 MiB); AOSS QMP
+ *          "load_state adsp on" and CX at its maximum level (qcom_q6v5_prepare + the proxy power domain), then
+ *          AUTH_AND_RESET. The ADSP's SMP2P item 443 entry "slave-kernel" says fatal (bit 0), ready (1),
+ *          handover (2); ours (item 429) carries "master-kernel". SMP2P doorbell: apss_shared+0xc bit 10.
+ *   GLINK  the "lpass" SMEM edge (remote pid 2, partition 0<->2): descriptor 478 and FIFO 479 are ours, FIFO 480
+ *          the ADSP's; doorbell bit 8. The ADSP opens "apr_audio_svc"; we answer and give it 20 x 512-byte
+ *          reusable intents (qcom,intents = <512 20>). Other channels it opens are logged and left alone.
+ *   APR    over that channel, apps (domain 5) -> adsp (4): AVCS core 3 (ready query), AFE 4, ASM 7, ADM 8.
+ *   Path   AFE clock QUAD_MI2S_IBIT (48 kHz x 2 x 16 bit = 1.536 MHz, CPU master as sdm845.c), I2S config of
+ *          QUATERNARY_MI2S_RX (0x1006: SD0, stereo, WS internal), DEVICE_START; ASM session 1 maps the ring (one
+ *          region; apps_smmu SID 0x1821, its low nibble in address bits 32..35 as q6asm-dai does), OPEN_WRITE_V3
+ *          multichannel PCM, ADM COPP on the port (NULL_COPP_TOPOLOGY) + matrix map, MEDIA_FMT, RUN, then
+ *          WRITE_V2 period by period, each re-queued when WRITE_DONE for an earlier one comes back.
+ *   Amps   TAS2559 (0x4c, left) + TAS2560 (0x4d, right) on QUP0 SE5's pins 85/86, bit-banged as the touch bus
+ *          (this SE's firmware is GSI-only); resets GPIO 12/76; their firmware tas2559_uCDSP.bin is parsed and
+ *          loaded by sweet_tas2559.c. They power up after the I2S clocks run and go down before they stop.
+ *
+ * Ring (SweetAudioABI.h): 16 periods of 512 stereo 16-bit frames, write-combined, mapped read/write into the
+ * client; frame f of the stream lives at (f % 8192) * 4. Three periods are queued at the DSP; a consumed period
+ * is zeroed (so a client that stops writing gives silence) and frames_done/host_time advance in the status
+ * page, which the plug-in turns into zero timestamps. STOP keeps the path running on silence; it is torn down
+ * after kern.sweet_audio_idle_s (15) idle seconds.
+ *
+ * Firmware (kept out of git): /usr/standalone/firmware/sweet/adsp.mbn and tas2559_uCDSP.bin (the beryllium images
+ * of the sdm845-mainline firmware-xiaomi-beryllium repo). Numbers and sequences from Linux
+ * drivers/remoteproc/qcom_q6v5_pas.c + qcom_q6v5.c, drivers/soc/qcom/smp2p.c + apr.c,
+ * drivers/rpmsg/qcom_glink_native.c + qcom_glink_smem.c, sound/soc/qcom/qdsp6 (q6afe, q6adm, q6asm, q6core,
+ * q6asm-dai, q6routing), sound/soc/qcom/sdm845.c, the sdm845/beryllium device trees and the phone's live DT
+ * (GPL-2.0: numbers and sequences only, no code copied); the SMEM/SMP2P/GLINK/QMP mechanics follow
+ * beryllium_wlan.c's modem edge.
+ */
